          <div class="description">
            Welcome to my app. Planet Tracker explores the scale and motion of the Solar System. The images are displayed at a large size to help visualise and better understand the immense distances involved.
            To put this into perspective, if Planet Earth were the size of a pea, our Solar System would be about 3.5 metres across. If the Solar System were then reduced to the size of a pea, the Milky Way galaxy would be roughly the size of Europe. If that entire galaxy were reduced to the size of a pea, the observable universe would be roughly the size of the Earth.

Beyond that lies the rest of the universe, whose true size remains unknown and may extend far beyond anything we can currently measure.
